  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">Actividad de Justicia</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Dexis Consulting Group</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(El Salvador):  The Justice Project aims to improve the independence, integrity, capacity, and oversight of the criminal justice system. It increases the scale, reach, and quality of people-centered justice (PCJ) services for victims of crime and people accused of crimes.The Justice Project will use FY 2024 funds to strengthen the investigative capabilities of the Public Defender&apos;s Office (PGR); harmonize how judges evaluate evidence at trial; and streamline the PGR&apos;s victim assistance services. The activity will help the PGR design an organizational plan and training curriculum for new hires incorporating a PCJ approach, and expand an internship program with law schools to address cases stemming from the State of Exception. The activity will train judges to fulfill their role in guaranteeing due process, support the reestablishment of ethics commissions at justice agencies, establish court user committees for citizen oversight, and implement a complaint system to strengthen judicial integrity. It will support civil society to establish CSO  committees to analyze justice trends, implement victim and survivor centered approaches, which put the rights and dignity of victims and survivors at the forefront of assistance and care; and promote improved coordination among groups working on similar issues. This activity contributes to MO 2.2 of the ICS, &quot;Promote the rule of law and equal access to justice,&quot; and Pillar II of the RCS, &quot;Combating corruption, strengthening democratic governance, and advancing the rule of law&quot; by improving the criminal justice system&apos;s performance in solving serious crimes, including by placing a new emphasis on the justice and security needs of individuals and communities, avoiding further backsliding in the rule of law</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">El proyecto aumentar&#xe1; la escala, el alcance y la calidad de los servicios de justicia centrados en las personas para las v&#xed;ctimas de delitos y las personas acusadas de delitos. Lo har&#xe1; fortaleciendo las capacidades de investigaci&#xf3;n de la defensa p&#xfa;blica y brindando servicios de asistencia jur&#xed;dica en los lugares seleccionados. El proyecto tambi&#xe9;n racionalizar&#xe1; y fortalecer&#xe1; los servicios de asistencia a las v&#xed;ctimas existentes empleando metodolog&#xed;as centradas en las v&#xed;ctimas e informadas sobre el trauma. El proyecto apoyar&#xe1; la integridad del proceso penal fortaleciendo la &quot;etapa de instrucci&#xf3;n&quot; y promoviendo la coordinaci&#xf3;n a nivel local a trav&#xe9;s del sistema local. Por &#xfa;ltimo, el proyecto apoyar&#xe1; a la sociedad civil aplicando el enfoque de acci&#xf3;n colectiva para formalizar la participaci&#xf3;n de la sociedad civil como organismo de control de la independencia y la transparencia judiciales.</narrative>
  </description>
